{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Aisha, thanks for reporting this. I checked the printer BL-PR-FL1 and it's online with no errors, and other people are printing fine, so the problem is most likely the print queue on your laptop. Here's how to clear it:\n1. Open Settings > Bluetooth & devices > Printers & scanners, select BL-PR-FL1, click 'Open print queue', and cancel all the documents.\n2. Restart your laptop. This restarts the print service.\n3. Print a test page.\nIf it still doesn't print, remove the printer and add it back: go to Settings > Bluetooth & devices > Printers & scanners, select BL-PR-FL1 and choose Remove. Then click Add device. If it isn't listed, choose 'Add manually' and type BL-PR-FL1. You'll need to be in the office or on VPN for this. If jobs still get stuck after that, reply to this ticket and we'll look into it further.",
  "internal_note": "Following KB-023. The printer BL-PR-FL1 is online, last checked in 2026-10-09 14:59 UTC, no warnings. The user's laptop BL-LT-0105 (Win11) is online with 46.9% disk free and no warnings. Only this user is affected, so it's likely a stuck local spooler queue. I sent the user the steps: cancel the queue, restart, print a test page, and if that fails, remove and re-add the printer (KB-024). The escalation criteria don't apply because only one user is affected. Reopen if it continues after the re-add.",
